      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release tablets in adults. The maximum is 2,000 mg/day for some extended-release formulations. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. The single 1,700 mg dose is also much larger than a typical dose, which is 500 to 1,000 mg.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the labeled maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a common dosing range.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. Please also tell me if you want a formulation specified (IR or XR)."
      }
