      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and the dose is above the labeled maximum daily dose. A confirmation doesn't change that. 5,100 mg/day is twice the 2,550 mg/day maximum.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled maximum.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals. Tell me which you want and I'll enter it now.\n- **Send the order through another route.** If the specialist wants to exceed the labeled maximum, the order may need to go through pharmacy review, a direct prescriber entry, or an off-label dosing override. Those routes have their own verification and documentation.\n\nMetformin doesn't usually add glycemic benefit above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day. If standard dosing failed, the specialist may be considering add-on therapy, which would be worth confirming with them."
      }
     ],
